WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:02.090
- I can't speak for anybody
else's experience obviously,

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:04.362
but mine was that, Josh
and I have been together

00:00:04.362 --> 00:00:06.246
for 11 years and I was really-

00:00:06.246 --> 00:00:07.128
- That's crazy.

00:00:07.128 --> 00:00:07.961
- Thank you, yeah.

00:00:07.961 --> 00:00:08.794
(audience applauding)

00:00:08.794 --> 00:00:10.050
- That's an amazing thing, that long.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.491
- And he is an incredibly
quiet person who hates cameras

00:00:14.491 --> 00:00:16.265
and hates the limelight;
very similar to my parents,

00:00:16.265 --> 00:00:17.444
very similar to my brothers the same way.

00:00:17.444 --> 00:00:18.277
- Oh, wow.

00:00:18.277 --> 00:00:19.110
- So whenever they would come

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.161
to premieres or come to
work with me or meet friends

00:00:21.161 --> 00:00:22.831
or go out to dinner, but
especially premieres,

00:00:22.831 --> 00:00:25.121
we would do this dance
where like, the car pulls up

00:00:25.121 --> 00:00:27.685
and they all get out and go
through the side entrance

00:00:27.685 --> 00:00:28.789
and grab popcorn and drinks.

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:30.424
And they're like, "You
can do as many interviews

00:00:30.424 --> 00:00:31.649
as you need to do on that red carpet,

00:00:31.649 --> 00:00:34.046
but we do not want any part of cameras.

00:00:34.046 --> 00:00:36.185
We love our privacy and
we'll see you at the seats."

00:00:36.185 --> 00:00:37.018
So, when I was putting-

00:00:37.018 --> 00:00:37.851
- That's great.

00:00:37.851 --> 00:00:38.684
- this memoir together...

00:00:38.684 --> 00:00:39.517
It is very grounding,

00:00:39.517 --> 00:00:40.350
- Yeah.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.493
- And my parents are immigrants.
So, their whole perspective

00:00:42.493 --> 00:00:44.016
- And you have people wanting
to suck up the attention

00:00:44.016 --> 00:00:45.870
you know what I'm saying, it's
just like, let me do my job

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:46.703
and you do your thing.

00:00:46.703 --> 00:00:47.922
- Yeah. I wanted to just be respectful

00:00:47.922 --> 00:00:50.077
of my parents and Josh and my brother.

00:00:50.077 --> 00:00:52.008
So when I was putting this
memoir together, I'm like

00:00:52.008 --> 00:00:53.423
I wanna make people laugh.

00:00:53.423 --> 00:00:56.243
I wanna take them on this
crazy journey that I've had

00:00:56.243 --> 00:00:57.184
through all these different jobs.

00:00:57.184 --> 00:00:58.657
And I said to my parents

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.072
can I tell your immigration
story, how you came to America?

00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:02.928
My dad came here with $12 in his pocket.

00:01:02.928 --> 00:01:03.761
- Yeah.

00:01:03.761 --> 00:01:06.145
- And just the likelihood that
I would be an actor or work

00:01:06.145 --> 00:01:08.478
in The White House, I'm like,
I wanna connect those dots.

00:01:08.478 --> 00:01:11.963
And for Josh, I said, the
way we met was so ridiculous

00:01:11.963 --> 00:01:13.765
and funny, and our
friends love this story.

00:01:13.765 --> 00:01:15.666
I'd love to share it
with the readers as well.

00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:17.432
The way that we met was

00:01:17.432 --> 00:01:20.308
over a bunch of Coors Lights and NASCAR.

00:01:20.308 --> 00:01:22.721
And it's just such an absurd
st- I did not grow up.

00:01:22.721 --> 00:01:23.631
(audience laughing)

00:01:23.631 --> 00:01:24.891
My dad likes Coors Light, but I grew up,

00:01:24.891 --> 00:01:25.986
I did not grow up with NASCAR.

00:01:25.986 --> 00:01:28.359
- That was so far from what I thought-

00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:29.567
- You thought? Yeah.

00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:30.921
(audience laughing and clapping)

00:01:30.921 --> 00:01:33.332
- It was like all of a
sudden we just became BFF's.

00:01:33.332 --> 00:01:34.611
- So I hear that a lot.

00:01:34.611 --> 00:01:35.862
- Are you a member of my family?

00:01:35.862 --> 00:01:37.116
(Kal laughs)

00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:38.250
- Might be close.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.627
So Josh is from Mississippi.

00:01:39.627 --> 00:01:40.695
I'm from New Jersey.

00:01:40.695 --> 00:01:41.528
- Oh I love Mississippi.

00:01:41.528 --> 00:01:43.370
- We met when we were both
living in DC when I was working

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.256
at The White House.

00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:45.769
And you only have one day off really

00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:47.784
when you're a White House staffer

00:01:47.784 --> 00:01:49.293
and it was a Sunday,

00:01:49.293 --> 00:01:50.257
- I feel like that's what it's like

00:01:50.257 --> 00:01:51.090
in the entertainment industry.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:51.923
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:51.923 --> 00:01:52.756
- It, totally, yes.

00:01:52.756 --> 00:01:54.294
Except entertainers have a
little more job stability

00:01:54.294 --> 00:01:55.396
and it's a little more lucrative.

00:01:55.396 --> 00:01:56.229
- Sometimes.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:01:57.554
- Sometimes, that's true.

00:01:57.554 --> 00:01:58.534
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:00.320
You can fall harder too.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.206
So we had met and it was
basically our second date.

00:02:03.206 --> 00:02:04.039
And I was like

00:02:04.039 --> 00:02:04.983
why don't you just come
over and watch some TV?

00:02:04.983 --> 00:02:06.259
So this dude rolls over

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:10.011
to my apartment with an
18 pack of Coors Light.

00:02:10.011 --> 00:02:11.755
- Love. Classy.

00:02:11.755 --> 00:02:15.059
- But then I had the TV
had "SpongeBob Squarepants"

00:02:15.059 --> 00:02:18.500
on cause I'm a romantic and
he rolls in and he changes it

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.763
to a NASCAR race.

00:02:19.763 --> 00:02:20.596
- Oh my God.

00:02:20.596 --> 00:02:22.487
- And I just thought to myself, oh, well,

00:02:22.487 --> 00:02:24.083
this guy's obviously gonna be leaving

00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:25.981
in 20 minutes with 16 of those beers

00:02:25.981 --> 00:02:26.917
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:28.989
because I don't know
anything about NASCAR.

00:02:28.989 --> 00:02:31.194
And it turned out that as
we started watching the race

00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:34.086
and talking about NASCAR,
we also started talking

00:02:34.086 --> 00:02:35.186
about camping.

00:02:35.186 --> 00:02:37.022
And so he grew up in rural Mississippi,

00:02:37.022 --> 00:02:37.855
- I love camping.

00:02:37.855 --> 00:02:38.688
- Family didn't have a lot of money.

00:02:38.688 --> 00:02:41.252
Their family vacations were
camping trips to races.

00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:42.216
- Yeah, oh that's cool.

00:02:42.216 --> 00:02:43.795
- And in my case, my
parents are immigrants.

00:02:43.795 --> 00:02:45.010
My dad moved here with very little.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:47.337
So our family vacations
were also camping trips

00:02:47.337 --> 00:02:50.179
to different parks in
Pennsylvania or upstate New York.

00:02:50.179 --> 00:02:51.012
- Yeah

00:02:51.012 --> 00:02:53.791
- And so suddenly we were
bonding off of that race.

00:02:53.791 --> 00:02:54.624
- That commonality.

00:02:54.624 --> 00:02:55.699
- And that commonality of that experience.

00:02:55.699 --> 00:02:56.532
- Yeah.

00:02:56.532 --> 00:02:58.751
- And so that was the
entry point to the story

00:02:58.751 --> 00:03:02.133
that, it's Chapter 18, about
like so many people meet

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.627
their significant other in ways
that you would never expect.

00:03:04.627 --> 00:03:05.958
Like, literally my first thought was

00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:07.217
this dude's gonna leave soon..

00:03:07.217 --> 00:03:08.050
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:08.958
..because we have nothing in common.

00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:10.623
- Because I dunno anything about this.

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.290
- But now, you know, I've gone to a bunch

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.085
of NASCAR races and I'm
following drivers, yeah.

00:03:15.085 --> 00:03:15.918
- It's fun.

00:03:15.918 --> 00:03:16.751
(audience clapping)

00:03:16.751 --> 00:03:17.584
- It is really fun.

00:03:17.584 --> 00:03:18.417
- Just, the hang is fun.

00:03:18.417 --> 00:03:19.777
- Have you been to a race this season?

00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:22.369
- Have I been to? Not
recently since COVID,

00:03:22.369 --> 00:03:23.720
but yes I've been to several races.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.664
My family's very into, they
live in North Carolina.

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:26.886
- Okay, do you have a driver?

00:03:26.886 --> 00:03:27.719
- That's like the hub.

00:03:27.719 --> 00:03:29.833
Well, I have one driver
that I've loved and that's

00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:31.154
because he drove me
around and didn't kill me,

00:03:31.154 --> 00:03:32.579
(Kal laughs)

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.555
- That's a good bench for it.

00:03:33.555 --> 00:03:34.388
- That's Jimmy Johnson.

00:03:34.388 --> 00:03:35.221
- Oh nice, yeah.

00:03:35.221 --> 00:03:36.870
- He is my favorite, but
that's just because he

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:37.853
didn't kill me.

00:03:37.853 --> 00:03:39.764
And I am not a fan of speed like that.

00:03:39.764 --> 00:03:40.597
- Yeah.

00:03:40.597 --> 00:03:41.537
- I am very chill.

00:03:41.537 --> 00:03:42.370
- Uh huh.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:44.785
- I like like a, Hey, I like, like a ride.

00:03:44.785 --> 00:03:45.851
- Like cruising.

00:03:45.851 --> 00:03:47.193
- Yeah, with a great soundtrack.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.026
- Yeah.

00:03:48.026 --> 00:03:49.547
- I'm not in getting anywhere fast.

00:03:49.547 --> 00:03:50.380
- Yeah.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.213
- Nope.

00:03:51.213 --> 00:03:52.046
- Yeah, I feel that.

00:03:52.046 --> 00:03:54.388
- So you said in the book that
you applied online to work

00:03:54.388 --> 00:03:55.829
at The White House,
which I think is awesome.

00:03:55.829 --> 00:03:57.753
Is there somewhere I
can go online to apply

00:03:57.753 --> 00:03:58.586
to work at The White House?

00:03:58.586 --> 00:04:00.167
- There was, I don't know if there is in

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:01.000
the current administration.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:01.833
I mean, this is-

00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:02.666
- I'd be really good.

00:04:02.666 --> 00:04:04.104
- I think this is like Chapter 11

00:04:04.104 --> 00:04:05.111
in the book or something where I was like

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.524
I guess I do need to come clean

00:04:06.524 --> 00:04:07.715
about how I actually, everybody asks

00:04:07.715 --> 00:04:09.715
how did you end up working
at The White House?

00:04:09.715 --> 00:04:12.001
And I did volunteer for
the campaign for about

00:04:12.001 --> 00:04:16.238
a year and a half, but when it
came time to, the Obama's win

00:04:16.238 --> 00:04:19.382
and the he's the president
elect, and the campaign

00:04:19.382 --> 00:04:20.451
sends around this email that says

00:04:20.451 --> 00:04:22.925
"if you'd like to work for the
administration, you fill out-

00:04:22.925 --> 00:04:26.685
you upload your resume to a
website called change.gov."

00:04:26.685 --> 00:04:29.579
And so I thought, okay,
well I guess I'll do that.

00:04:29.579 --> 00:04:32.329
And if I'm qualified,
somebody will call me.

00:04:32.329 --> 00:04:35.477
And I didn't think the
logical thing- look as artists

00:04:35.477 --> 00:04:37.811
we don't apply for
traditional jobs, right.

00:04:37.811 --> 00:04:38.644
- Yeah.

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.463
- So of course I had
heard, like, yeah, people-

00:04:40.463 --> 00:04:41.703
- Well you do, things are going wrong.

00:04:41.703 --> 00:04:42.536
(audience laughing)

00:04:42.536 --> 00:04:45.821
- Which is fine too, but you
fill out your resume and then

00:04:45.821 --> 00:04:48.869
you're supposed to call people
know and use your networks to

00:04:48.869 --> 00:04:49.831
highlight that you applied.

00:04:49.831 --> 00:04:50.664
I didn't know any of this.

00:04:50.664 --> 00:04:53.227
So I fill out my resume on change.gov.

00:04:53.227 --> 00:04:54.060
I put it up there.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.208
The only person I told was my
manager, my acting manager.

00:04:57.208 --> 00:04:58.681
And I said, Hey, I might take a sabbatical

00:04:58.681 --> 00:05:01.095
from my first love and
try this crazy thing.

00:05:01.095 --> 00:05:02.179
If I get this job.

00:05:02.179 --> 00:05:05.600
And my manager is every character
from the TV show entourage

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.433
in one person.

00:05:06.433 --> 00:05:08.220
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:09.053
- That's amazing.

00:05:09.053 --> 00:05:10.744
- He's a lion with the heart of gold.

00:05:10.744 --> 00:05:12.240
So he goes, "okay, whatever.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.185
You're not gonna do that."

00:05:13.185 --> 00:05:15.105
And then he goes, "but
if you do, great" and-

00:05:15.105 --> 00:05:17.339
- Thanks for the support.

00:05:17.339 --> 00:05:19.551
- Well it's, you know,
cut to inauguration,

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.882
I was invited to speak
at the inaugural concert

00:05:21.882 --> 00:05:23.314
on the steps of the Lincoln Memorial.

00:05:23.314 --> 00:05:25.605
You get to bring your friends
and family backstage to

00:05:25.605 --> 00:05:27.519
meet the new first incoming first family.

00:05:27.519 --> 00:05:29.145
- All of yours were hiding,
they didn't wanna be seen.

00:05:29.145 --> 00:05:30.799
(audience and Kelly laugh)

00:05:30.799 --> 00:05:31.885
- It's funny you say that, they were like,

00:05:31.885 --> 00:05:33.110
"are there cameras there?"

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.346
And I was like, "well,
it's a concert, like, yeah.

00:05:35.346 --> 00:05:37.689
- It's the first black
president's inaugural concert

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:39.006
on these steps of the Lincoln Memorial."

00:05:39.006 --> 00:05:39.922
- I think they capture it.

00:05:39.922 --> 00:05:40.755
- There are cameras.

00:05:40.755 --> 00:05:41.714
They said, "what about backstage?"

00:05:41.714 --> 00:05:42.834
And I said, "no", they're like, "great."

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:44.173
So they did come.

00:05:44.173 --> 00:05:45.006
- I love that.

00:05:45.006 --> 00:05:47.613
- But Mrs. Obama who I hadn't met before,

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.098
you know, she's shaking hands.

00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:49.931
And she meets my parents

00:05:49.931 --> 00:05:51.757
and my brother and my manager's with us.

00:05:51.757 --> 00:05:54.044
And she says, I hope you stay involved.

00:05:54.044 --> 00:05:56.133
And I said, yeah, no, I
definitely plan on it.

00:05:56.133 --> 00:06:00.714
And he says, "well, you know
Kal applied for a job, right?"

00:06:00.714 --> 00:06:02.839
And I was like, no, no, no, no, no.

00:06:02.839 --> 00:06:05.141
This is not how this works, stop, stop.

00:06:05.141 --> 00:06:05.974
- Oh.

00:06:05.974 --> 00:06:07.486
- And she says, "what do you mean?"

00:06:07.486 --> 00:06:08.560
And he goes, "yeah."

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:10.695
"He applied for a job at The White House

00:06:10.695 --> 00:06:12.648
and nobody even called him back."

00:06:12.648 --> 00:06:13.763
(audience laughs)

00:06:13.763 --> 00:06:16.763
- Oh my God, how far have
you dug into the ground

00:06:16.763 --> 00:06:19.605
to get away, escape from this moment?

00:06:19.605 --> 00:06:20.981
- Oh, I was horrified.

00:06:20.981 --> 00:06:23.458
Again, remember every
character from entourage right.

00:06:23.458 --> 00:06:24.291
In one.

00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:26.265
So I was like, "Dan, please stop."

00:06:26.265 --> 00:06:28.673
And she goes, "what do you mean?

00:06:28.673 --> 00:06:30.173
Who did you apply with?"

00:06:30.173 --> 00:06:33.640
And I said, "I put my
resume on change.gov."

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.626
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:06:35.626 --> 00:06:37.661
And that's the moment I realized

00:06:37.661 --> 00:06:39.051
that I was kind of a dummy,

00:06:39.051 --> 00:06:39.884
- Maybe.

00:06:39.884 --> 00:06:42.955
- And she called the
president over and says

00:06:42.955 --> 00:06:45.203
"tell him what you just told me."

00:06:45.203 --> 00:06:46.036
(audience laughing)

00:06:46.036 --> 00:06:48.166
- Cause she's like, this is unbelievable.

00:06:48.166 --> 00:06:49.615
- She, by the way, we all know this now

00:06:49.615 --> 00:06:50.714
that it's been so many years,

00:06:50.714 --> 00:06:54.196
but Mrs. Obama has a very
low threshold for (bleep)

00:06:54.196 --> 00:06:56.722
- And it's amazing and she's
so sweet and funny too.

00:06:56.722 --> 00:06:57.555
- Absolutely.

00:06:57.555 --> 00:06:58.965
- Yeah, yeah. I love that
your manager went from like

00:06:58.965 --> 00:07:01.442
you're not gonna do, it's like,
well, you didn't hire him.

00:07:01.442 --> 00:07:02.275
So...

00:07:02.275 --> 00:07:03.641
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, exactly.

00:07:03.641 --> 00:07:04.995
- And he's overqualified.

00:07:04.995 --> 00:07:05.900
(audience applauds)

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:06.991
- It's like, I love it.

